# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# CourtCoach AI – Environment Variables
# Copy this file to `.env.local` and fill in the values.
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Supabase project URL (found in: Supabase Dashboard → Project Settings → API)
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://<project-ref>.supabase.co

# Supabase anonymous (public) key — safe to expose in the browser
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=<your-anon-key>

# Public URL of this deployment (used for magic-link redirect URLs)
# In development: http://localhost:3000
# In production:  https://your-app.vercel.app
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=http://localhost:3000

# Anthropic API key — SERVER ONLY. Never prefix with NEXT_PUBLIC_.
# Used exclusively by POST /api/chat to call Claude claude-sonnet-4-5.
# Obtain at: https://console.anthropic.com/account/keys
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...

# ── Google OAuth (optional — magic-link works without this) ───────────────────
# Set to "true" once you have completed ALL three steps below.
# When absent or "false", the "Sign in with Google" button is hidden and the
# login page falls back gracefully to magic-link only — no errors.
#
# Steps to enable Google OAuth:
#
#  1. Google Cloud Console  (https://console.cloud.google.com)
#     a. Create (or select) a project.
#     b. APIs & Services → Library → enable "Google Calendar API".
#     c. APIs & Services → OAuth consent screen:
#        • User Type: External (or Internal for Workspace orgs)
#        • Add scope: https://www.googleapis.com/auth/calendar.readonly
#        • Add your domain to Authorized domains.
#     d. APIs & Services → Credentials → Create Credentials → OAuth Client ID:
#        • Application type: Web application
#        • Authorized redirect URIs — add EXACTLY:
#          https://<project-ref>.supabase.co/auth/v1/callback
#          (replace <project-ref> with your Supabase project reference)
#        • Copy the resulting Client ID and Client Secret.
#
#  2. Supabase Dashboard  (https://supabase.com/dashboard)
#     Authentication → Providers → Google:
#     • Toggle "Enable Google provider" ON.
#     • Paste the Client ID and Client Secret from step 1d.
#     • Save.
#
#  3. Set the env var below to "true" and redeploy.
#
NEXT_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_OAUTH_ENABLED=false
